    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "A most attractive period redbrick townhouse located on historical street in centre of Drogheda town. Built around 1880, the property was further extended to provide ample accommodation ideal for town centre living. On entering, you are greeted by a large entrance hall with original coving, high ceilings and original staircase. Off the hall are 2 reception rooms, the 1st being a beautiful light filled space with bay windows and original coving. The 2nd living room is to rear with potential to interconnect both. On passing through hall, a rear hall leads to large bathroom and also the kitchen. A nice square well proportioned room, the kitchen has patio doors leading to large private rear garden. Upstairs, a half landing leads to 1st bedroom and 2nd bathroom. The first floor comprises of 2 extra large bedrooms. \r\nThis style of property has become extremely popular with buyers now seeing all the advantages of town centre living. No.2 gives a complete blank canvas for purchaser to use their creative spirit to transform this wonderful property. We note also that this type of property and location would lend itself to use in professional practice or other alternative uses (subject to planning).\r\n\r\nDescription from www.buildingsofireland.ie:\r\nThis attractive house, forming an integral part of a formally-planned terrace, is a good example of developments in residential architecture towards the end of the nineteenth century. Brick detailing and the corniced canted bay window are typical of architectural tastes in the late-Victorian era and fine cast-iron gates and railings, another characteristic feature, add a note of artistic interest, enhancing the building's overall appearance.\r\n\r\nEntrance Hall: 9.2 x 1.54\r\nOriginal coving, original staircase, cloakroom\r\nSitting room: 4.84 x 4.54\r\nOriginal solid wood floor, bay windows with plantation blinds\r\nLiving room: 4.2 x 3.79\r\nCast iron fireplace\r\nRear Hall: 3.52 x 1.02\r\nBathroom: 2.36 x 1.02\r\nBath, wc, whb, hotpress\r\nKitchen: 4.08 x 3.72\r\nFitted units, patio door to garden\r\nHalf Landing\r\nShower room: 2.2 x 1.42\r\nElectric shower, wc, whb\r\nBedroom 1: 3.49 x 3.39\r\nOriginal wood floor\r\n1st Floor\r\nBedroom 2: 3.76 x 3.69\r\nFitted wardrobes, plantation shutters\r\nBedroom 3: 5.78 x 3.87\r\nFitted wardrobes, plantation shutters\r\n\r\nFeatures:\r\n1. Oil fired central heating\r\n2. Large private rear garden/patio\r\n3. Mix of wood and upvc windows\r\n4. Commercial fire alarm system\r\n5. Internal fire doors\r\n6. Many original features"
      },
      {
